,title,link,text,language,family
0,Warao language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warao_language,"Warao is the Native language of the Warao people. A language isolate, it is spoken by about 33,000 people primarily in northern Venezuela, Guyana and Suriname. It is notable for its unusual object–subject–verb word order.",Warao,Language isolate
1,Warao language,https://grokipedia.com/page/Warao_language,"The Warao language is recognized as a language isolate, a natural language with no demonstrable genetic relationship to any other language family, based on the absence of regular sound correspondences, shared morphological patterns...",Warao,Language isolate
2,Warao Language (WBA) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/wba/,Warao is a stable indigenous language of Venezuela and Guyana. It is an isolate that is not known to be related to any other language. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.,Warao,Language isolate
3,Ethnomusicology as Advocacy: The Warao of Venezuela,https://dolsenmusic.com/ethnomusicology-as-advocacy-the-warao-of-venezuela/,"warao4 Today the Warao number approximately 19,500 individuals grouped into about 250 villages throughout the central Orinoco Delta. The most isolated and also the most “traditional” Warao are those who live in the central delta of the Orinoco, on the Winikina River.",Warao,Language isolate
4,Warao: An interesting and curious language isolate.,https://www.endangeredlanguages.com/resource/warao-interesting-and-curious-language-isolate,"Language. Warao. Resource Type. Video.The video is entirely in English, which contains several written examples of Warao, but at no point does he attempt to speak it, likely to avoid the danger of butchering the pronunciation.",Warao,Language isolate
