6,"Warao Language and the Warao Indian Tribe (Guarao, Warau, Warrau)",https://www.native-languages.org/warao.htm,"Warao Language: Linguistics article on Warao including information on language usage, syntax, and bibliography. Warao Language: Warao information from Indigenous Languages of the Caribbean.",Warao,Language isolate
7,Comparison: Warao vs. Warray – Languages with Wilf,https://languageswithwilf.wordpress.com/2019/02/17/comparison-warao-vs-warray/,"In alphabetical order, our first language is Warao, a language isolate spoken by around 33,000 in the Orinoco Delta of north-eastern Venezuela, alongside smaller communities in the nearby countries of Trinidad and Tobago, Guyana and Suriname.",Warao,Language isolate
8,Warao Bible | Bibles International,https://biblesint.org/languages/warao,"The literacy rate among the Warao men is 60%, significantly higher than the 42% literacy rate among women. Recognized as a language by the Indigenous Languages Law of 2008, Warao boasts extensive documentation and university-level teaching.",Warao,Language isolate
